; 43g: the zone BIND serves to rdnsd over XFR-over-TLS (RFC 9103) and over
; nothing else. Its `allow-transfer transport tls` in bind-primary.conf is what
; makes a successful transfer proof that the transfer was encrypted: a
; cleartext AXFR of this zone is refused by the primary, so a secondary holding
; it cannot have got it in clear.
$TTL 3600
@       IN SOA ns1.fromxot.test. hostmaster.fromxot.test. ( 2026091201 3600 600 604800 300 )
@       IN NS  ns1.fromxot.test.
ns1     IN A   10.53.0.7
www     IN A   198.51.100.70
